# What the core format makes of branches.sderiv (the specification, "Conformance"): the program as its
# fingerprint, its canonical form and its normal form, and its values at fixed points with
# the interpreter, in hexadecimal, in either compute type. SEISSOL_EXPR_GOLDEN=write writes it
# anew from what the interpreter of the build gives.
fingerprint = a7f3ea1c5f343a1e
canonical form
| expr1 ct8
| grid 0 inline\x1flinear\x1fclamp\x1fstatic\x1fdata:2:12:3405440600732518926
| 0=field i0
| 1=const 3fe0000000000000
| 2=pw lt 0 1
| 3=field i1
| 4=const 0000000000000000
| 5=pw lt 3 4
| 6=lookup 0:0 0 3
| 7=lookup 0:1 0 3
| 8=pw select 5 6 7
| 9=pw abs 0
| 10=const 3ff0000000000000
| 11=pw add 9 10
| 12=pw sqrt 11
| 13=pw abs 3
| 14=const 4000000000000000
| 15=pw add 13 14
| 16=pw div 12 15
| 17=const 4008000000000000
| 18=pw add 13 17
| 19=pw sqrt 18
| 20=const 4010000000000000
